        </div>
        <h3>Narration and shot list</h3>
        <p class="build-note">A short version for a recorded walkthrough. The article is the complete reference; the list is not a separate claim.</p>
        <ol class="build-shotlist">
          <li><strong>Open on the finished profile.</strong> “This is a real profile, four links, one guestbook invitation and one approved note.” Show desktop then phone.</li>
          <li><strong>Explain the two jobs.</strong> “Guestbook owns the note and the review. Linkarooie owns the profile and the choice to feature it.”</li>
          <li><strong>Show the brief and the Init spec.</strong> “The starting composition is portable data. It does not grant deployment authority.”</li>
          <li><strong>Show the change.</strong> “The source now answers one question: does this exact Guestbook accept a postcard right now?”</li>
          <li><strong>Submit the note.</strong> Show the real form, the pending receipt and the private state.</li>
          <li><strong>Approve and feature.</strong> Show the Guestbook page, then the separate Linkarooie featuring step and card.</li>
          <li><strong>Hide at source.</strong> Refresh the profile. “The card and media are gone; the source still owns the record.”</li>
          <li><strong>Close the Guestbook.</strong> Refresh. “No button, no dead form. The profile explains the state.” End on the source links and the local run procedure.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>
